<title>VENEZUELA: Sivensa launches class B ADRs.</title>
<headline>Sivensa launches class B ADRs.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan steel company Siderugica Venezolana Sivensa said its Class B American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) would start trading Monday.</p>
<p>The level one ADRs are backed by five Class B Sivensa shares, which opened trade at 306.50 bolivars.</p>
<p>Sivensa's class B shares only differ from Class A shares in that they do not carry full voting rights.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 834405</p>
</text>
